Subject: .moddata version 2, wrapper revision 2, kabi and compiler-pin checks

A module's .moddata is now version 2 (amix-dlm
docs/contracts/C3-1-module-object.md): word 0 as before, "MD2\0", then
NUL-terminated key=value strings ending with an empty one.  The core
checks every key's syntax, refuses an unknown key that starts with '!',
and checks the module against this kernel: the name is the file's, the
kabi family and major are the kernel's and the minor not above it, the
compiler pin is the kernel's, and a core-tier module carries the
kernel's build id.  The kernel's kabi and pin come from the kernel build
(DLM_KABI, DLM_PIN in dlmconf.c), its build id from plat_dmainit().
Dependencies come from the depend key.  The wrapper revision is 2, so a
revision-1 core refuses these modules and this core refuses revision 1.
Root class is refused until the arena load path exists.  mkmod writes
version 2 from the Master's keys and -K/-P; modfix checks the marker;
the state harness and test/run.sh gain the C3-1 refusals (modfix -1
lets the version-1 refusal case through).  30-module-core.md section
2, patch 4.

